# What EAS uploads to its build machines.
#
# By default the EAS CLI uploads what git would archive, which is wrong for this project: every
# asset the app needs — the game itself, the icon, the splash — is gitignored, because
# `npm run sync` writes them out of the repository root's build rather than committing them. A
# cloud build without this file arrives with no icon, no splash and no game, and fails or ships a
# diagnostic screen.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore entirely for uploads — it is not additive. So this is a copy of
# .gitignore with the five `assets/` lines removed. Keep the two in step when either changes.

node_modules/
.expo/
dist/

# Regenerated in the cloud by `expo prebuild` on every build. This is a Continuous Native
# Generation project; uploading a local copy is pointless at best and stale at worst.
/android/
/ios/

# The store submission kit: screenshots, icons and listing text for the two consoles. Generated
# by `yarn store:kit`, uploaded by hand to Play and App Store Connect, and of no use whatsoever
# to a build machine. This is the one line that is deliberately NOT in .gitignore.
store/

# Local output of scripts/ios.mjs — the archive and .ipa from a Mac build. Never needed remotely.
build/
